  "id": "Compound::DB00812 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Phenylbutazone is likely to interact with Slc22a11 through a shared mechanism involving organic anion transport. The evidence suggests that Phenylbutazone binds to Slc22a8 or Slc22a6, which then participate in organic anion or cation/anion/zwitterion transport. This transport process is ultimately mediated by Slc22a11, as indicated by the hierarchical participation relationships. The varying scores across the paths suggest that Phenylbutazone's interaction with Slc22a8 or Slc22a6 may lead to similar downstream effects on Slc22a11, reinforcing the notion of a functional link. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc22a11 in facilitating the transport of organic ions, potentially through the same or related transporters. The evidence supports a mechanism where Phenylbutazone influences Slc22a11 via a shared transport pathway, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
